    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 43\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 4877, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  in  relation  to  legalizing,  validating,  ratifying  and\n      confirming certain transportation contracts of  the  Corning  city\n      school district\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 6289, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\n      Monticello  central school district notwithstanding the failure to\n      timely file final building cost reports with the education depart-\n      ment\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 6356-B, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      transportation  contracts  for  the  Baldwin  Union  Free   school\n      district\"\n\nAssembly Bill Number 6360-B, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      transportation  contracts for the West Hempstead Union Free school\n      district\"\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nSenate Bill Number 396-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a transportation contract of the Oneonta city school district\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 1798, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\n      Panama central school  district  notwithstanding  the  failure  to\n      timely  file  the  final  building cost reports with the education\n      department\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 1867, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a transportation contract of the Fulton city school district\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 4963-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT relating to validating certain acts by the Pearl River union\n      free school district  relating  to  final  building  cost  reports\n      required to be filed with the state education department\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 6188-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a certain contract of the West Islip union free school district\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  These  nine  bills  would forgive certain violations of state law that\nresulted in the repayment or withholding of expense-based  building  aid\nand  transportation  aid  that  would  have otherwise been owed to these\nschool districts.\n \n  Payment of expense-based aids to school  districts  is  calculated  as\npart  of  the  state's  annual budget process. Because these bills would\nalter the aids agreed to in the Enacted State  Budget  for  the  current\nyear, I am constrained to veto these bills.\n \n  Previously,  action has been taken to address these types of aid with-\nholdings in several  past  State  Budgets.  Legislation  in  2011  ended\nprepayment  of  building  aid  without  final  cost reports, so that new\nbuilding aid clawbacks could no longer occur, and the Fiscal  Year  2013\nEnacted  State  Budget  provided  amnesty for prior projects. The Fiscal\nYear 2018 and Fiscal Year 2019 budgets also limited annual building  aid\nwithholding amounts and eliminated residual penalties for districts with\nhigh  penalties as a percentage of operating budget. I welcome a conver-\nsation with the Legislature as part of  the  upcoming  state  budget  to\naddress  these  aid withholdings once and for all, and to ensure the law\nfairly reflects consequences to school districts.\n \n  The bills are disapproved.                     (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
